  {
   "id": 198980,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Your new boss doesn’t have a pension or 401(k) plan for your retirement, but she agrees to place aside $12,000 every year once a year for four years. She gives you the option of either starting immediately on your first day of work or starting one year from now. That makes this the difference between an ordinary annuity and an annuity due. If the plan earns 5% per year, compounded annually, what will be the difference between the two approaches after the four years / four payments?",
